<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Limbdi State</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Limbdi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Jhala Rajput state in Saurashtra whose ruler hosted Swami Vivekananda in 1891, one of the middle-ranking states of the Kathiawar Agency.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The ruling family belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jhala">Jhala Rajput</a> clan, which also ruled <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dhrangadhra-state">Dhrangadhra</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/wankaner-state">Wankaner</a>, and tradition dates its rule at Limbdi to around 1500. Firm records begin later.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Limbdi was an agricultural state in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jhalawad">Jhalawad</a> region, known for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a>. Its Thakore Sahebs were noted for promoting education, and Thakore Jaswantsinhji hosted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swami-vivekananda">Swami Vivekananda</a> during his travels in 1891.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Limbdi joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saurashtra-state">United State of Saurashtra</a> in 1948 and is now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/surendranagar-district">Surendranagar district</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/limbdi-state.jpg" alt="Limbdi State" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: Dr. Andreas Birken at German Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SaurashtraKart.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Limbdi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jaswantsinhji</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>India</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Limbdi</dd></dl></aside></div>
